summary:
- topic: Meeting Start and Announcements
  text: The meeting began with a roll call and the Pledge of Allegiance. Upcoming
    dates were announced, including the next regular school board meeting on June
    10th and the last day of school on June 13th.
- topic: Personnel Resignations
  text: The board acknowledged the resignations of BrianCavanaugh (Assistant Director
    of Instructional Support), AmyBrier (Kindergarten teacher at Small), and AngelaCorcoran
    (Grade 1 teacher at Kaler), wishing them well in their future endeavors.
- topic: Personnel Appointments
  text: Several new personnel elections were presented, including AnnaBolton (English
    at SPHS), SarahGlenn (Principal at SPHS), MeghanHenderson (Kindergarten at Brown),
    CollinMagarian (Grade 4 at Brown), HermenegildoPaulo (Director of Diversity, Equity,
    and Inclusion), and ShelbySantor (Grade 1 at Dyer).
- topic: New Principal and DEI Director Introductions
  text: SarahGlenn, the new SPHS Principal, expressed excitement for her new role,
    emphasizing the district's 'you belong here' motto. HermenegildoPaulo, the new
    Director of Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion, shared his enthusiasm for driving
    change and supporting the district's vision.
- topic: Board Comments on New Hires
  text: Board members expressed excitement and welcomed the new appointees, noting
    their positive reputations in the community and the opportunity for growth and
    expansion within the district.
- topic: Public Comment Period
  text: A brief public comment period was held for topics on the agenda, but no citizens
    came forward to speak.
- topic: Executive Session for Collective Bargaining
  text: The board voted unanimously to enter into an ExecutiveSession to discuss collective
    bargaining with the SouthPortlandSchool Department ServiceEmployeesAssociation,
    as per 1MRSA§405(6)(D).
